1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:06,244
Welcome to Episode Eleven, an extended lesson on SMT Divergence.

2
00:00:06,664 --> 00:00:17,680
We will walk through bullish and bearish case studies step by step, compare each with an alternative where SMT fails, and then look at market conditions that change its reliability.

3
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,412
Step one: Instrument A approaches its previous low.

4
00:00:23,832 --> 00:00:29,880
Step two: Instrument B approaches its corresponding previous low, at the same time.

5
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:35,676
Step three: Instrument A trades below its previous low, a lower low.

6
00:00:36,096 --> 00:00:41,712
Step four: Instrument B does not make a corresponding lower low. It holds above.

7
00:00:42,132 --> 00:00:50,508
Step five: highlight the discrepancy. The vertical lines show the same two swings, at the same times, on both charts.

8
00:00:50,928 --> 00:00:58,848
Step six: label it a potential bullish SMT divergence. Potential, because nothing is confirmed yet.

9
00:00:59,268 --> 00:01:06,036
Step seven: confirmation appears in Instrument A, as price closes above the last lower high.

10
00:01:06,456 --> 00:01:10,176
Step eight is the alternative, and it deserves its own look.

11
00:01:11,996 --> 00:01:16,844
Here is the alternative. Both instruments trade below their previous lows.

12
00:01:17,264 --> 00:01:22,640
There is no disagreement, so there is no SMT, and both continue lower.

13
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:28,100
When related instruments confirm each other, continuation is the simpler reading.

14
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:35,224
The bearish case. Step one: Instrument A approaches its previous high.

15
00:01:35,644 --> 00:01:40,300
Step two: Instrument B approaches its corresponding previous high.

16
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:45,040
Step three: Instrument A trades above its previous high.

17
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:50,044
Step four: Instrument B fails to make a corresponding higher high.

18
00:01:50,464 --> 00:01:55,360
Step five: the discrepancy is marked at the same swings on both charts.

19
00:01:55,780 --> 00:02:00,124
Step six: potential bearish SMT divergence.

20
00:02:00,544 --> 00:02:06,352
Step seven: confirmation in Instrument A, a close below the last higher low.

21
00:02:06,772 --> 00:02:14,044
Step eight: the alternative, where both instruments make higher highs and continue higher. No SMT.

22
00:02:15,864 --> 00:02:20,688
In the bearish alternative, both instruments break their previous highs together.

23
00:02:21,108 --> 00:02:26,220
Agreement means no SMT. Do not search for a divergence that is not there.

24
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:38,024
SMT reliability depends on conditions. Between strongly correlated instruments, divergence is unusual, so it carries more information.

25
00:02:38,444 --> 00:02:43,916
Between weakly correlated instruments, divergence is common, so it tells you little.

26
00:02:44,336 --> 00:02:50,288
Correlations change over time. Yesterday’s relationship may not hold today, so recheck it.

27
00:02:50,708 --> 00:02:57,308
Different session hours can produce false divergences, when one instrument is closed or thinly traded.

28
00:02:57,728 --> 00:03:04,352
News can hit one instrument harder than the other. That divergence is fundamental, not hidden strength.

29
00:03:04,772 --> 00:03:09,716
And some divergences are temporary, resolving quickly without consequence.

30
00:03:11,536 --> 00:03:20,872
Finally, a divergence that does not lead to a reversal. A makes a lower low while B holds a higher low: a genuine bullish SMT.

31
00:03:21,292 --> 00:03:27,628
But A never shifts structure. Both instruments resume falling, and B eventually breaks its low too.

32
00:03:28,048 --> 00:03:39,184
A real divergence, and no reversal. That is exactly why confirmation on A matters, and why SMT interpretation weakens when the relationship is unstable.

33
00:03:41,004 --> 00:03:47,988
To summarise. Use the eight steps, and always look at the alternative. Agreement means no SMT.

34
00:03:48,408 --> 00:03:56,376
Reliability depends on how strong and stable the relationship is. Session hours and news can create false divergences.

35
00:03:56,796 --> 00:04:00,516
And a divergence without confirmation is only a warning.

36
00:04:02,336 --> 00:04:08,072
Time to check your understanding. Pause the video and answer these five questions in your own words.

37
00:04:09,992 --> 00:04:15,416
